+	       call is what makes this reachable from a link-only invocation:
+	       see tcc_eh_frame_adopt_output().  Whether tcc GENERATED unwind
+	       tables for code it compiled (-f[no-]asynchronous-unwind-tables)
+	       does not enter into it -- what decides the header is whether the
+	       merged output has .eh_frame content to index, from wherever.
+	       Measured on x86-64, GNU ld 2.44 and gold alike: a final link
+	       emits .eh_frame_hdr and PT_GNU_EH_FRAME whenever merged
+	       .eh_frame content exists, emits neither when no input carried
+	       any, and never emits one under -r (which does not reach this
